  {
    "label": "86dec134-c288-5f12-9971-6b0570d7076d",
    "record": {
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "86dec134-c288-5f12-9971-6b0570d7076d",
        ":question/problem": "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x)=\\frac{3-9\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{5}?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-9\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{5}=-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-\\frac{9}{5}.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=|-\\frac{9}{5}|=\\frac{9}{5}.$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "367782f4-ca15-5206-b0f9-015103d3f79a",
